# The task vocabulary

`go-task` is the only thing a developer or a CI job invokes — never __RAW_TOOLS__
directly. `tools/lint/check_ci_entrypoint.py` enforces this for every CI
definition; nothing enforces it for a developer's shell, because the
vocabulary being smaller and more memorable than the tools underneath it is
the actual incentive.

## Top-level tasks

| Task | Does |
|---|---|
| `task setup` | Install both workspaces and any local runtime dependencies |
| `task validate` | The aggregate gate — `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` |
| `task lint` | Every lint: backend, frontend |
| `task format` | Format Python and frontend code, in place |
| `task typecheck` | Static type-check the backend and frontend |
| `task test` | Backend and frontend test suites |
| `task dev` | Backend + frontend dev servers, in parallel |
| `task clean` | Remove build outputs and caches |

## Namespaced tasks

| Namespace | Example | Does |
|---|---|---|
| `api:*` | `task api:dev` | The backend process alone |
| `web:*` | `task web:dev`, `task web:test` | The frontend workspace alone |
| `quality:*` | `task quality:lint:backend` | Internal — the lint/test/typecheck primitives the top-level wrappers compose |

Run `task --list` for the full, current surface — this page is a map, not
the source of truth for what exists.
